hadiths[2]{hadithnumber,text}:
"22332","Abdullah narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Abu Dawud al-Hafari narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Abu Ishaq, from Matar ibn Ukamis, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When Allah decrees the death of a servant in a land, He makes for him a need to go to it."
"22333","Abdullah narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Jafar al-Warkani narrated to us, Hudayj Abu Sulayman narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Matar ibn Ukamis, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: It is not decreed for anyone to die in a land except it is made beloved to him and a need for him to go to it is made."
